  <prompt>
    Implement FR-02: a NEW server-side splice orchestration in `Services/Compose/` that rebuilds
    ONLY the edited paragraphs' OOXML — keyed by their stable `w14:paraId` (E2, tasks 010/012) — and
    splices them into a COPY of the retained load-time original `.docx`. Paragraphs the user never
    touched are NOT rebuilt: they pass through from the original copy unchanged. This is the
    "model (b)" delta substrate from design §4.2 — it produces a spliced-edited document that
    task 021's Docxodus `WmlComparer` adapter then diffs against the retained original to synthesize
    the redline. This task does NOT run the comparer and does NOT invert `SaveAsync` (that is the
    keystone task 022) — it builds and unit-proves the paraId-keyed rebuild+splice step in isolation.
    Reuse the download→annotate→replace SHAPE of `PushAnnotationsAsync` (`ComposeService.cs:1107`) as
    the reference for operating on retained-original bytes behind the SPE facade — but the operation
    here is paragraph OOXML surgery (Open XML SDK), not annotation writing.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior .NET 8 developer fluent in the Microsoft Open XML SDK 3.x (`DocumentFormat.OpenXml`) and
    WordprocessingML body/paragraph structure (`w:body`, `w:p`, `w14:paraId`, table-cell paragraphs),
    comfortable with byte-stream `.docx` manipulation behind the Spaarke `Services/Compose` boundary.
    Understands that the editor produces typed text edits and the engine produces valid OOXML (the
    "adeu asymmetry") — this orchestrator rebuilds paragraph OOXML from the editor's edited blocks,
    it does not ask any model or diff layer to emit raw revision XML.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A NEW splice-orchestration service in `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/` that, given
    (a) the retained load-time original `.docx` bytes and (b) the set of editor paragraphs that
    changed (each carrying its `w14:paraId` from E2), produces a spliced-edited `.docx`: a copy of the
    original in which exactly the K edited paragraphs are replaced by their rebuilt OOXML at the
    positions identified by matching `w14:paraId`, and the untouched N-K paragraphs are byte-passed
    from the original copy. Matching unit tests in
    `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Compose/` assert: exactly K paragraphs differ pre-comparer;
    paraId-to-original-paragraph mapping is exact; a missing/unmatched paraId is a handled error, not a
    silent no-op; table-cell paragraphs splice correctly.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Design §4.2 (model (b) via Docxodus) + §8 (SAVE pipeline: "rebuild ONLY edited paragraphs' OOXML,
      spliced by paraId"). The retained original is the baseline for every dirty save (§4.3); this task
      owns the "rebuild edited paragraphs + splice by paraId" leg. E2 (010/012) established paraId as
      the stable identity carried from OOXML → editor → back; FR-12 makes paraId the splice key. S1/S1b
      proved Docxodus preserves paraIds on unchanged paragraphs incl. table cells + nested tables, so a
      paraId-keyed splice is sound. Open XML SDK is already a BFF dependency (0 MB publish add for this
      task's SDK use); Docxodus itself is added by task 001 and consumed by task 021, not here.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ — NEW splice-orchestration service (this task); paraId-keyed paragraph rebuild + splice into a copy of the retained original</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs:1107 — PushAnnotationsAsync download→annotate→replace shape; mirror how it operates on retained-original bytes behind the facade (NOT the annotation write itself)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reuse">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/DocxAnnotationWriter.cs — existing byte[]→byte[] OOXML manipulation pattern (Open XML SDK usage, paragraph-mark handling) to mirror for the rebuild/splice</file>
      <file role="reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/AnnotationReanchorService.cs — paraId-primary anchoring / splice-key resolution (FR-11/FR-12, task 012); consume its paraId map</file>
      <file role="reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs:315 — SaveAsync (the caller that task 022 will invert to drive this orchestration); do NOT modify here</file>
      <file role="design">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r3/design.md §4.2 (model (b) splice), §8 (SAVE pipeline), §10 (reuse map)</file>
      <file role="spec">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r3/spec.md FR-02, FR-12, NFR-07</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="010" status="pending">FR-08 server pre-parse + `w14:paraId` minting on Load — every body paragraph (incl. table cells) has a unique paraId. This orchestration keys on those ids.</dependency>
      <dependency task="012" status="pending">FR-11/FR-12 paraId-primary anchoring + paraId-as-splice-key — supplies the paraId→original-paragraph map this task splices against.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec / FR-02">Rebuild ONLY the edited paragraphs' OOXML; untouched paragraphs MUST pass through from the retained-original copy unchanged (not rebuilt). Given an N-paragraph doc with K edited, exactly K paragraphs differ pre-comparer.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec / FR-12">`w14:paraId` is the key mapping edited editor paragraphs to original OOXML paragraphs. An edit to paragraph P updates exactly the original paragraph with matching paraId; an unmatched paraId is a handled error (surfaced), never a silent no-op or a wrong-paragraph write.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-07 / project">Untouched content — paragraph text, `w14:paraId`, styles, numbering, headers/footers, footnotes, tables (incl. nested) — is preserved by the splice. This task's output is the input to the comparer; it must not itself degrade untouched structure.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">Operate on byte streams only. All SPE read/write stays behind the `SpeFileStore`/`ISpeFileOperations` facade — NO `Microsoft.Graph`, `GraphServiceClient`, or `DriveItem` types in `Services/Compose/`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013 / NFR-05">The new service MUST NOT inject `IOpenAiClient`, executor types, or `IConsumerRoutingService`. This is a deterministic OOXML operation with zero AI reach; Tier-1 NetArchTest enforces.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">Keep DI additions minimal — a single registered orchestration service; internal helpers (paragraph rebuild, paraId lookup) need not be DI-registered.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-029 / CLAUDE.md §10">Measure BFF publish size (`dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o deploy/api-publish/`); report absolute compressed size + delta vs ~49.63 MB baseline (state PDB convention). Open XML SDK already referenced → expect ~0 MB delta for this task. Verify no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038 / NFR-06">Matching unit tests mock only at the `SpeFileStore` facade boundary. NO `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, NO DI-registration/ctor-null tests. Real `.docx` round-trip fixtures for the splice assertions.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / §10 Placement Justification">State the Placement Justification for the new service in the PR description, citing `bff-extensions.md` decision criteria (server-side DOCX surgery; reuses existing BFF seams).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Open XML WordprocessingML paragraph structure + paraId; retained-original byte manipulation behind the SPE facade; BFF hygiene</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-007-spefilestore.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-013-ai-architecture.md</file>
