    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Retained-original delta shape" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs:1107">
        PushAnnotationsAsync download→annotate→replace — mirror how it fetches retained-original bytes and produces new bytes behind the facade; substitute paragraph rebuild+splice for the annotation write.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Byte[]→byte[] OOXML manipulation" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/DocxAnnotationWriter.cs">
        Open XML SDK open-document / edit-body / save pattern with paragraph-mark handling; reuse the SDK usage shape for the paragraph splice.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + dependency check">Confirm tasks 010 + 012 seams (paraId map + splice-key resolution) are available. Output the FULL rigor-level declaration. Load the knowledge files + bff-extensions.md; state the Placement Justification before designing.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Define the edited-paragraph input contract">Define the structured input the orchestration consumes: the retained-original bytes + the set of edited editor paragraphs, each carrying its `w14:paraId` + its rebuilt content. Reuse the E2 paraId map / compose edit-payload shape where it aligns; do not invent a parallel schema. Keep the DTO in `Services/Compose/`.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Implement paraId-keyed rebuild + splice">Open a COPY of the retained-original with the Open XML SDK; build a `w14:paraId → w:p` index over the body (incl. table-cell paragraphs). For each edited paragraph, locate the original `w:p` by paraId and replace it with the rebuilt OOXML in place; leave all other paragraphs untouched. Handle an unmatched paraId as a surfaced error. Produce the spliced-edited bytes.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Unit tests">Author tests in `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Compose/`: given an N-paragraph fixture with K edited, assert exactly K paragraphs differ vs the original pre-comparer; assert paraId mapping is exact (edit to P touches only P); assert a table-cell paragraph splices correctly; negative — an unmatched/missing paraId surfaces an error and does NOT write the wrong paragraph.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Verify + size/CVE report">Build BFF + run the new tests. Run publish-size + CVE, report absolute + delta vs ~49.63 MB. Run the Tier-1 NetArchTest facade check (no AI-internal injection in Services/Compose). Update TASK-INDEX status.</step>
  </steps>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ (NEW splice-orchestration service + input DTO)</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/ComposeModule.cs (register the new service, unconditional)</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Compose/ (splice + paraId-mapping tests)</output>
    <output type="report">Publish-size absolute + delta vs ~49.63 MB; CVE scan result; Placement Justification</output>
  </outputs>

  <justification>
    <existing>No existing service rebuilds + splices paragraph OOXML by paraId. `DocxAnnotationWriter` writes redline/comment markup (annotation direction); `ComposeService` is the SPE-lifecycle facade; `AnnotationReanchorService` resolves anchors but does not perform OOXML paragraph surgery. Verified by Grep over `Services/Compose/` — no overlap.</existing>
    <extension>Cannot be folded into `DocxAnnotationWriter` (annotation-authoring responsibility) or `ComposeService` (SPE lifecycle, SRP): the paraId-keyed rebuild+splice is a cohesive, heavily-unit-tested OOXML concern that is the input stage to the comparer (task 021) — a distinct unit warranting its own testable service.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without a paraId-keyed splice, the delta save (022) has no way to produce a spliced-edited document that preserves untouched paragraphs while carrying the K edits — FR-02 acceptance ("exactly K paragraphs differ pre-comparer") and the whole model-(b) delta substrate (§4.2) cannot be met; dirty saves stay lossy.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">Given an N-paragraph `.docx` with K paragraphs edited, the orchestration produces a spliced-edited document in which exactly K paragraphs differ from the retained original pre-comparer; the other N-K are unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Edited paragraphs are located and replaced by matching `w14:paraId`; an edit to paragraph P updates exactly the original paragraph with matching paraId (unit test asserts the mapping).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Untouched paragraphs pass through unchanged — text, `w14:paraId`, styles, numbering, and structural parts (headers/footers, footnotes, tables incl. nested) are preserved through the splice (NFR-07 structural/semantic).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A table-cell paragraph is spliced correctly by its paraId (S1b nested/table-cell case).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: an edited paragraph whose `w14:paraId` matches no original paragraph surfaces a handled error and does NOT silently no-op or overwrite the wrong paragraph.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`Services/Compose/` injects no AI-internal type (Tier-1 NetArchTest green); no `Microsoft.Graph` type appears in `Services/Compose/` (ADR-007).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish size reported absolute + delta vs ~49.63 MB baseline, ≤60 MB (expect ~0 MB delta — Open XML SDK already referenced); no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Matching unit tests exist and pass (mocked only at the SpeFileStore facade); BFF build is green.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>
</task>
